17592186518703 1071 "The least common multiple of $7(w+1)$ and $8(w+1)$ is {{field-1}}. Use the positive integer LCM of the contents and a primitive polynomial part with positive leading coefficient." 13194139535576 17592186045443 true] [17592186518703 1072 #uuid "d824e1a1-5d65-5398-9e0a-160d4d776848" 13194139535576 17592186045443 true] [17592186518703 1074 "To find the least common multiple ($\\text{LCM}$) of two polynomials that are made up of products of binomials, we find the least common multiple of the constants and the least common multiple of the variable part. Then, we multiply all of the results together.\n\nSo first, we find $\\text{LCM}(7,8):$\n\n- Multiples of $7:$ $\\,7,\\,14,\\,21,\\,28,\\,35,\\,42,\\,49,\\,56,\\,63,…$\n\n- Multiples of $8:$ $\\,8,\\,16,\\,24,\\,32,\\,40,\\,48,\\,56,\\,64,…$\n\nSo, $\\text{LCM}(7,8)=56.$\n\nSince the variable part is the same in the expressions, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{LCM}((w+1),\\,(w+1))=(w+1).\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply all of our results together:\n\n$$\n\\text{LCM}(7(w+1),\\,8(w+1))=56\\cdot (w+1)=56(w+1).\n$$" 13194139535576 17592186045443 true] [17592186518704 1075 #edb/ref 17592186518694 13194139535576 17592186045443 true] [17592186518704 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139535576 17592186045443 true] [17592186518704 1077 "field-1" 13194139535576 17592186045443 true] [17592186518704 1078 #edb/ref 17592186518694 13194139535576 17592186045443 true] [17592186518704 1079 #uuid "db16543e-b333-5210-adb8-66a17c9f10ca" 13194139535576 17592186045443 true] [17592186518705 1075 #edb/ref 17592186518679 13194139535576 17592186045443 true] [17592186518705 1075 #edb/ref 17592186518698 13194139535576 17592186045443 true] [17592186518705 1075 #edb/ref 17592186518702 13194139535576 17592186045443 true] [17592186518705 1075 #edb/ref 17592186518708 13194139535576 17592186045443 true] [17592186518705 1075 #edb/ref 17592186518709 13194139535576 17592186045443 true] [17592186518705 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139535576 1759218