7592186045443 true] [17592186518711 1071 "The least common multiple of $-18t^{2}-12t-54$ and $-42t^{2}-28t-126$ is {{field-1}}. Use the positive integer LCM of the contents and a primitive polynomial part with positive leading coefficient." 13194139535576 17592186045443 true] [17592186518711 1072 #uuid "f04fc474-2b81-5526-b7b3-963927d357e5" 13194139535576 17592186045443 true] [17592186518711 1074 "To find the least common multiple ($\\text{LCM}$) of two polynomials that differ by a constant factor, we find the least common multiple of the constants and the least common multiple of the variable part. Then, we multiply all of the results together.\n\nFirst, factor out the integer contents and identify the common primitive polynomial:\n\n$$\n-18t^{2}-12t-54=(-6)(3t^{2}+2t+9),\\qquad -42t^{2}-28t-126=(-14)(3t^{2}+2t+9).\n$$\n\nUse the positive contents $6$ and $14$.\n\nSo first, we find $\\text{LCM}(6,14):$\n\n- Multiples of $6:$ $\\,6,\\,12,\\,18,\\,24,\\,30,\\,36,\\,42,\\,48,…$\n\n- Multiples of $14:$ $\\,14,\\,28,\\,42,\\,56,…$\n\nSo, $\\text{LCM}(6,14)=42.$\n\nSince the variable part is the same in the expressions, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{LCM}((3t^{2}+2t+9),\\,(3t^{2}+2t+9))=(3t^{2}+2t+9).\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply all of our results together:\n\n$$\n\\text{LCM}(-18t^{2}-12t-54,\\,-42t^{2}-28t-126)=42\\cdot (3t^{2}+2t+9)=42(3t^{2}+2t+9).\n$$" 13194139535576 17592186045443 true] [17592186518712 1068 #edb/ref 17592186518676 13194139535576 17592186045443 true] [17592186518712 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535576 17592186045443 true] [17592186518712 1071 "Find the least common multiple of $-48x^{2}+60x+48$ and $-32x^{2}+40x+32.$ Use the positive integer LCM of the contents and a primitive polynomial part with positive leading coefficient." 13194139535576 17592186045443 true] [17592186518712 1072 #uuid "f5be060c-9236-5ca1-9c00-95b0c2fa5264" 13194139535576 17592186045443 true] [17592186518712 1074 "To find the least common multiple ($\\text{LCM}$) of two polynomials that differ by a constant factor, we find the least common multiple of the constants and the least common multiple of the variable part. Then, we multiply all of the results together.\n\nFirst, factor out the integer contents and identify the common primitive polynomial:\n\n$$\n-48x^{2}+60x+48=(-12)(4x^{2}-5x-4),\\qquad -32x^{2}+40x+32=(-8)(4x^{2}-5x-4).\n$$\n\nUse the positive contents $12$ and $8$.\n\nSo first, we find $\\text{LCM}(12,8):$\n\n- Multiples of $12:$ $\\,12,\\,24,\\,36,…$\n\n- Multiples of $8:$ $\\,8,\\,16,\\,24,\\,32,…$\n\nSo, $\\text{LCM}(12,8)=24.$\n\nSince the variable part is the same in the expressions, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{LCM}((4x^{2}-5x-4),\\,(4x^{2}-5x-4))=(4x^{2}-5x-4).\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply all of our results together:\n\n$$\n\\text{LCM}(-48x^{2}+60x+48,\\,-32x^{2}+40x+32)=24\\cdot (4x^{2}-5x-4)=24(4x^{2}-5x-4).\n$$" 13194139535576 17592186045443 true] [17592186518713 1080 "15(y+9)^{2}" 13194139535576 17592186045443 true] [17592186518713 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535576 17592186045443 true] [17592186518713 1083 #uuid "fbf9a564-7479-5cfa-b465-fe463632b33e" 13194139535576 17592186045443 true] [17592186518714 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186152116.py" 13194139535576 17592186045443 true] [17592186518714 1169 #uuid "fdf8c4f2-b537-5750-811e-bf7c82d1e6b0" 13194139535576 17592186045443 true]] :edb/tempids {"082992d9-37a2-5282-8195-8305c381cbe6" 17592186518668 "0cddac94-1754-5ee7-828d-6cb21f0e5443" 17592186518669 "1da352d1-9cc2-5ab4-b3e9-15254ff4f874" 17592186518670 "293301bb-138a-52be-8ea4-6c5fd3e5e824" 17592186518671 "2bde1693-f779-5c80-87c3-a6883bd959d3" 17592186518672 "2d987246-413c-500f-84a8-2c88b0b408f2" 17592186518673 "4440328e-eff4-5ec9-b0c9-747251dc5b27" 17592186518674 "44d969f8-8e86-543f-a3f6-503e8d8e20d9" 17592186518675 "49a39293-a5d2-521d-8585-942acbe96905" 17592186518676 "51a4b442-b209-5164-a118-6ee86d68fd3d" 17592186518677 "53523790-ad90-56a7-a601-57c70739d7b3" 17592186518678 "5591b804-1d51-5139-9875-f61ec45eddd4" 1